1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,917
One of the first

2
00:00:00,917 --> 00:00:02,836
and most exciting questions you'll answer

3
00:00:02,836 --> 00:00:04,421
is what do you want
to teach?

4
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:06,673
In California, arts credentials are divided

5
00:00:06,673 --> 00:00:08,925
into four distinct subject areas:

6
00:00:08,925 --> 00:00:12,137
Dance, Theater,
Music, and Visual Arts.

7
00:00:12,137 --> 00:00:13,888
Each is its own credential.

8
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:15,223
That means you'll be
credentialed

9
00:00:15,223 --> 00:00:18,226
in your specific discipline,
not just the arts generally,

10
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:21,271
which also means the pathway
may look a little different

11
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:23,148
depending on which one
you choose.

12
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:24,858
Some of these subject areas

13
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:27,027
have more credentialing programs

14
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:28,945
available statewide than others.

15
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:30,905
They might have different exam requirements

16
00:00:30,905 --> 00:00:32,866
or different demand
in the schools,

17
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:35,076
so it's worth knowing what
you're walking into.

18
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,953
If you're not sure
which one fits you best,

19
00:00:36,953 --> 00:00:38,955
Like if you work across multiple art forms,

20
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:40,248
just pick one to start with.

21
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:41,833
You can always go
back into the portal

22
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:43,418
to try alternate pathways

23
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:45,795
and decide which one feels best for you.
